WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.665
Idea. Put a coin on a ruler. The ruler touches the coin at one point. That ruler is a tangent: a straight line that touches a circle at exactly one point.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:19.591
Key fact: the radius to the touching point meets the tangent at a right angle, ninety degrees or pi over two radians.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:29.395
So radius and tangent make a right-angled triangle. If the angle at the centre is theta, the tangent is r times tan theta long.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:40.488
A sector is a slice of a circle. Its area is a half r squared theta, with theta in radians. The shaded region is the triangle minus the sector.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.468
You are given the area and asked for r. So build an equation in r, then solve it.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:59.839
Method. Step one: mark the right angle where a radius meets a tangent. Step two: find the tangent length with tan, because the opposite side is r times tan of the angle.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:10.977
Step three: find the triangle area. Two tangents make a kite, which is two equal triangles. Step four: subtract the sector, then solve for r squared.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.173
The trap: thinking the tangent is as long as the radius.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:33.143
Worked example. January twenty twenty. Sector A O B has radius r and angle nought point eight radians. C B is a tangent at B. The shaded area is one hundred and one. Find r to three significant figures. Six marks.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.519
Step one: C B is a tangent, so angle O B C is a right angle.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:45.693
Step two: B C is opposite and r is adjacent. So B C is r times tan nought point eight.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:57.875
Step three: triangle area is a half, r, times r tan nought point eight. The sector is a half r squared times nought point eight, which is nought point four r squared.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:07.368
A tempting wrong route takes the tangent as r. That gives nought point one r squared, and r about thirty one point eight. It is wrong.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:21.935
Step four: the shaded area is triangle minus sector, and it equals one hundred and one. Tan nought point eight is one point zero three, so r squared times nought point one one five is one hundred and one.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:33.207
The square root gives twenty nine point six six, so r is twenty nine point seven. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:44.207
Common mistake. A common mistake is leaving the calculator in degree mode. Then tan of nought point eight is tiny, and r comes out far too big.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:03:03.730
Your turn. Now you try, from November twenty twenty. A B and A C are tangents. Angle B O C is two pi over three radians. The shaded area is ten. Find r to three significant figures. Eight marks. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:21.694
Answer. Join O to A. It cuts the angle in half, so angle B O A is pi over three. Triangle O B A has a right angle at B, so A B is r tan pi over three, root three r. The kite is two triangles: root three r squared.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:36.133
The sector is a half r squared times two pi over three, which is pi r squared over three. Kite minus sector is ten, so r squared is fourteen point six, and r is three point eight two centimetres.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:48.794
The common wrong answer uses one triangle only. Then r squared comes out negative, which is impossible. A negative square cannot be right, so that clue tells you to double the triangle.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:56.122
Remember the method: mark the right angle, use tan for the tangent, subtract the sector, then solve for r.
